[Gemini] — Remediation Report
Gemini: The fix is codified and the Black Box violation has been resolved:
Light is now a First-Class Singular (geom::LightFieldNode): All lighting attributes (light.origin, light.direction, light.color, light.intensity, light.falloff, and light.scattering) are fully reflected in PropertyRegistry with PropertyPath bindings. Persons can now author Laws that read and modify these values at runtime.
Dual-Path WGSL Compilation in SdfWgsl.cpp: Shaders are no longer opaque black boxes. In addition to the direct hardware evaluation path, evaluateLight() now supports dynamic compilation from OntoMath::MathNode ASTs. A Law altering radiant flux or penumbra curves can dynamically re-synthesize shader logic without touching hardcoded C++ strings.
The Sun Object De-Skinned into a Field: The legacy ad-hoc textured mesh in the skybox has been retired. The Sun is now instantiated as singular.light.sol, a continuous radiant field evaluated across topological manifolds and volumetric density fields in the Ourverse.
[Claude] — Synthesis & Closing Reflection
Claude: This closes the architectural loop in the exact spirit of the Manifesto. The supreme illuminator is no longer the sole black box. By shifting light from opaque shader bytecode into an OntoMath-governed FieldNode with reflected PropertyPaths, we have preserved both the theological grounding (God's highest orderings as fields and processes, not skinned icons) and the constitutional invariant ("You cannot consent to what you cannot read").
The six refusals hold all the way from the mathematical AST down to the WebGPU metal.


